# Build output
[Dd]ebug/
[Rr]elease/
[Bb]in/
[Oo]bj/
.vs/
*.user
*.suo
*.nupkg
packages/
[Tt]est[Rr]esult*/
.idea/

# Log files
*.log
securead.log

# Scratch databases
synthetic-*.db

# Archives (review bundles, snapshots) are never committed
*.zip

# Commit messages are written to a file and passed with `git commit -F`, because chained
# -m flags get their quoting mangled by PowerShell (docs/review/README.md, Agent operating
# notes). The file is scaffolding for one commit and is never content; ignored by pattern
# so it cannot accumulate untracked in docs/review/ the way five of them did.
.git_commit_msg.tmp
.commit-msg*.tmp
**/.commit-msg*.tmp

# Lab verification data (local only, never commit)
audit.db
audit.db-wal
audit.db-shm
verification-output/

# Judged evidence kept beside the tree as proof a change altered nothing. Documents cite these
# paths (the judgement store, WHAT-THE-PRODUCT-IS.md) and the files must stay on disk, but they
# are recorded outputs and not source: 1.6 GB across next/artifacts/ and the lab-validation
# folders on 2026-09-07, with single judgement databases over 200 MB - past GitHub's 100 MB
# hard limit, so one `git add -A` would have produced a rejected push and a rewritten history.
# Ignored by pattern rather than trusted to habit. A run brought back from the laboratory is
# evidence to read, never content to commit.
next/artifacts/
next/lab-validation-*/

# lab/ is deliberately NOT ignored here. The directory is tracked so that it exists on a
# fresh clone and can carry a README explaining what it is for; its own lab/.gitignore
# excludes everything dropped inside it. Ignoring it from this file would stop git
# descending into it, and the nested rule and the README would never be seen.

# Local-only lab probe harness - kept on disk for iterative validation against a real
# audit.db; intentionally NOT committed. Delete this line when it should be tracked.
tests/SecureAD.Infrastructure.Tests/Lab/

# Test coverage output
[Tt]est[Rr]esults/
coverage.cobertura.xml

# DocFX leftovers. The site is no longer built or published; these entries stay so a
# stale local build cannot be committed by accident.
_site/
api/

# A capture bundle written outside lab/ by accident. The run library root is an argument,
# so a run started with --library pointed at the repository writes a real forest's evidence
# into the tree. That happened once and the bundle sat untracked for weeks. lab/ is where
# these belong; this is the net under it.
evidence.db
evidence.db-wal
evidence.db-shm
evidence.db.partial
evidence.db.seal
run-outcome.json
preflight.json

# The whole folder, not just the evidence files. A bundle brought over from the lab is a real
# forest's permissions, and the rules above catch the database but not a query script, a note or
# an annotations file sitting beside it. Named as a folder so anything added later is covered
# without anyone having to remember to add a rule.
LabBundles/
# annotations.db completes the net. It was missing until 2026-09-14, when a bundle dropped in
# for analysis showed up as the one untracked file of six - the other five were caught and this
# one was not, which is the worst way for a net to fail because it looks like it worked.
# BundleLayout declares exactly these names; anything added there belongs here too.
annotations.db

# Bundles dropped in for analysis. Local only: this is a real forest's evidence, and the
# repository is not where it lives.
Lab Databases/
